In the minimal $\Lambda	extrm{CDM}+\sum m_{
u}$ model with most recent CMB data from Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE, lowE, and lensing; and BAO data from BOSS DR12, MGS, and 6dFGS, we find that at 95\% C.L. the bounds are: $\sum m_{
u}<0.12$ eV (degenerate), $\sum m_{
u}<0.15$ eV (normal), $\sum m_{
u}<0.17$ eV (inverted). The bounds vary across the different mass orderings due to different priors on $\sum m_{
u}$.
